[38;2;124;124;124mActually, let me verify this construction works. The finest group topology on [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mF(X) making ι continuous - does this exist? [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mA group topology on F(X) is a topology making the group operations continuous. [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mWe want the finest such that ι is continuous. [0m

[38;2;124;124;124mConsider all group topologies τ on F(X) such that ι: X → (F(X), τ) is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mcontinuous. The intersection of all such topologies... no wait, we want the [0m
